NAME
    tail - print the last lines of a file or stdin

SYNOPSIS
    tail [-n N] [path]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the last N lines (default 10) of piped stdin, or a real file if
    <path> is given (walled to the project's own directory tree - see 'cd').
    No '-f' follow mode - this shell has nothing that appends to a file
    live while 'tail' is running to follow.

EXAMPLES
    history | tail -n 5
    tail notes.txt
